# <type>(<scope>)[!]: <subject>
# .cz.toml is the new-message validation owner. Scope and ! are optional.
# Ordinary authored messages require a supported type, nonempty scope when used,
# a nonblank subject, and a blank line before optional body/footer.
# Unicode, type capitalization and a final period are permitted by the grammar.
# Breaking changes use ! before the colon, a breaking footer, or both.
# .cz.toml defines exact generated Merge/Revert shapes; the paired hook guard
# rejects prefix-only spoofs. A manually authored matching shape also passes.
# These checks prove no Git generation, merge/revert or provenance, and grant no authority.
# Native Revert messages are accepted but excluded from the conventional changelog.
# Recommended: imperative and specific subject, preferably under 72 characters.
# Capitalization and body wrapping are recommendations, not enforced grammar.
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

# Explain why the change is needed when the subject does not make that clear.
# Optional footer examples:
# Closes #7
# BREAKING CHANGE: unowned namespaces are now denied
# BREAKING-CHANGE: unowned namespaces are now denied
# Bang example: feat(gitops)!: require namespace ownership
# Revert example: revert(gitops): restore the prior route
# The optional body can identify the reverted commit; do not rewrite history.
#
# Infrastructure examples (choose the smallest relevant scope):
# feat(gitops): add namespace ownership policy
# fix(qa): reject incomplete descendant cleanup
# refactor(qa): remove repeated harness validation
# style(shell): apply shared indentation
# docs(operations): explain local cluster recovery
# test(policy): cover missing namespace labels
# build(qa): pin validation dependencies
# ci(github): preserve failed QA in the summary
# perf(validation): reuse parsed document metadata
# chore(git): ignore generated validation output
# release: prepare version metadata
# deps(qa): update the pinned linter
